+# context-lifecycle
+
+## Requirement: Resilient teardown
+
+Flask SHALL attempt every registered request- and application-context teardown
+callback and teardown-signal receiver, even when an earlier teardown operation
+raises. It SHALL restore context-local state before propagating teardown errors.
+On Python versions with exception groups, all collected teardown errors are
+propagated together; otherwise, Flask may propagate the first collected error.
+
+### Scenario: Multiple teardown failures
+
+- WHEN more than one teardown callback or signal receiver raises while a
+  request or application context is popped
+- THEN later callbacks and receivers still run, context-local state is reset,
+  and the errors are raised after cleanup
+
+## Decisions
+
+- D-17: teardown failures are collected through cleanup; fail-fast teardown was
+  rejected because it can skip cleanup and leave context-local state active.
